From 7f8c727a2f0cdd95f6e7b80c2c2a8ea5709ea46b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreyKatzburg <64795827+CoreyKatzburg@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 04:48:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/17] Telemetry: zero-normal counts, top inward instances,
 and qpcMs join key

Worker E (problem 5, black and inside-out surfaces) needs to know which meshes have zero or invalid
normals and which instances face inward. The gate pass now also runs on static instances and counts
triangles with a zero or non-finite decoded normal (zeroNormalSkinnedTriangles/Instances,
zeroNormalStaticTriangles/Instances), and keeps a per-instance inward count so the recorder can list
the 8 most inward skinned instances (topInwardInstances: inward, tris, geomHash by the asset hash
rule so it matches USD capture mesh names, albedoHash, cull, flip, blend, enc).

qpcMs is QueryPerformanceCounter in ms, read on the D3D9 thread when a frame goes to ray tracing,
the same clock as d3d9_proxy_frames.csv column 2, so the two files can be cross-checked frame by
frame. Inherited inward/skinned fields are unchanged. Verified offline only: build and remix source
tests pass; the shader classification has not run live yet.
